===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|pocket-knife|pocket knife}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|pocket|knife}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pocketknives}}

# A [[knife]] small enough for carrying safely and [[handy|handily]] in a pocket; usually a {{l|en|folding knife}} (with [[blade]]s or [[tool]]s that the user can fold or [[retract]] into the [[handle]]).
#*{{quote-text|en|year=1878||author=Mark Twain|title=Tom Sawyer Abroad; About Magnanimous-Incident Literature|passage=Jimmy had a '''pocketknife''', and he wandered into the drawing-room with it one day, alone, and reduced ten thousand dollars' worth of furniture to an indeterminable value in rather less than three-quarters of an hour.}}
#*{{quote-text|en|year=1944||author=Alfred Lief|title=Camillus: The Story of an American Small Business |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=yZ3JAAAAMAAJ|passage=The Army, the Navy, the Maritime Commission, and Lend-Lease demanded more and more '''pocketknives''' &mdash; for demolition kits, medical kits, aviators’ kits, electricians’ kits; knives with tools, knives with marlin spikes. The '''pocketknife''' attained a new status &mdash; as indispensable equipment for all men in uniform.}}

